{
 "_about": "The token tree build_tokens.py turns into tokens.json. A leaf with \"var\" takes its value from that variable in css-vars.json, resolved on the host in \"owner\" (refero = refero.design, styles = styles.refero.design); a leaf with \"value\" carries a measured value and names the measurement in \"source\" (an entry of raw/measurements.md, components-computed.json or layout.json). Both hosts share one palette: the --gray-solid/-alpha/-glass scales, --fill-*, --stroke-*, --text-* and --status-* names mean the same thing on refero.design's `body` and styles.refero.design's `:root`, and the dark blocks (refero's body#dark-theme + body:not(#light-theme), styles' :root under prefers-color-scheme: dark) hold the same scale inverted. Where a name is declared twice the leaf notes which host supplied the value.",

